.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ECCE-QM, B3LYP/6-31G*, relaxed scan of the O=C-N-C torsion of N-methylacetamide, 360 to 0 degrees in 25 points. This calculation shows that the relaxed scan of nma_scan depends on its direction (hysteresis): run backwards, the energy rises to 92.0 kJ/mol at 240 degrees and drops to 20.3 kJ/mol at 225 degrees, the mirror image of the forward scan, because the nitrogen stays pyramidal on the higher-energy branch until it flips. The lower envelope of the two scans peaks near 58 kJ/mol at 90 and 270 degrees, and the true rotation barrier is below both curves.
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ECCE-QM
